WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.567
-Our first guest tonight
is a very funny actor,

00:00:02.567 --> 00:00:04.367
comedian, and
"Celebrity Jeopardy!" champion

00:00:04.367 --> 00:00:05.834
you know from
"The Mindy Project,"

00:00:05.834 --> 00:00:07.033
"Neighbors,"
and "The Afterparty."

00:00:07.033 --> 00:00:09.033
He executive-produces and stars

00:00:09.033 --> 00:00:10.667
in "History of the World,
Part II."

00:00:10.667 --> 00:00:13.934
New episodes premiere daily
through March 9th on Hulu.

00:00:13.934 --> 00:00:15.167
Let's take a look.

00:00:15.167 --> 00:00:17.501
-Aah!
[ Door opens ]

00:00:17.501 --> 00:00:18.701
[ Grunts ]

00:00:18.701 --> 00:00:22.334
Sorry I'm late, but I'm here now
in my uniform.

00:00:22.334 --> 00:00:25.167
Why don't we sign this treaty
and end this war?

00:00:25.167 --> 00:00:26.901
Alright?
Here we go.

00:00:26.901 --> 00:00:28.300
Right here.

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:29.634
Ah-ah-ah.

00:00:29.634 --> 00:00:32.167
Bobby, you're up.

00:00:32.167 --> 00:00:34.701
-This is truly
the most difficult thing

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:36.467
I have ever
been called on to do.

00:00:36.467 --> 00:00:37.567
-Just go ahead and sign it.

00:00:37.567 --> 00:00:39.834
-I pray that this never
happens again.

00:00:39.834 --> 00:00:40.834
-Right next to where I put mine.

00:00:40.834 --> 00:00:42.767
-As a boy,
my father taught me to --

00:00:42.767 --> 00:00:44.100
-What'd he tell you?
What'd he tell you?

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:47.033
You got to fight with a sign
to end the war.

00:00:47.033 --> 00:00:50.067
Huzzah!
Who wants a drink?

00:00:50.067 --> 00:00:51.467
I do.
You want a drink?

00:00:51.467 --> 00:00:53.267
You want a drink?
I'm buying, I'm buying.

00:00:53.267 --> 00:00:54.501
-Please welcome back to the show

00:00:54.501 --> 00:00:56.767
our very good friend
Ike Barinholtz, everybody!

00:00:56.767 --> 00:00:58.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:58.868 --> 00:01:07.133
♪♪

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:15.334
♪♪

00:01:15.334 --> 00:01:16.734
Great clip.
Great clip.

00:01:16.734 --> 00:01:19.667
We got our friend Jack McBrayer,
little -- my brother --

00:01:19.667 --> 00:01:21.601
-Little Josh Meyers in there.

00:01:21.601 --> 00:01:23.601
-Yeah, very nice, very exciting.
-Yes, yes, Civil War.

00:01:23.601 --> 00:01:25.901
Spoiler alert, the North won.

00:01:25.901 --> 00:01:28.300
-Okay. Thank you.

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:29.734
Thank you
for letting everybody know.

00:01:29.734 --> 00:01:31.667
I have so much
to talk to you about.

00:01:31.667 --> 00:01:33.734
Now, I want to get to
"Celebrity Jeopardy!"

00:01:33.734 --> 00:01:37.667
but I know that in order
to be considered a celebrity,

00:01:37.667 --> 00:01:39.367
you have to be --
it has to be worldwide,

00:01:39.367 --> 00:01:41.734
and you are now worldwide-known.

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:44.200
You just took a Christmas trip
to England.

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:45.400
-I did.

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:46.901
-Recognized there, as well,
I would assume.

00:01:46.901 --> 00:01:50.000
-I was recognized throughout
England, throughout France.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:51.234
-Wow.

00:01:51.234 --> 00:01:54.133
-I now call myself
Mr. Worldwide, like Pitbull.

00:01:54.133 --> 00:01:56.000
[ Laughter ]
-Does Pitbull know?

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:58.667
-No, he does not know, and don't
tell him, guys, seriously.

00:01:58.667 --> 00:02:01.133
Don't, like, tag, snitch me.

00:02:01.133 --> 00:02:04.501
So we went to England for --
We were there for the holidays.

00:02:04.501 --> 00:02:07.667
Right? And we were there
Christmas Day.

00:02:07.667 --> 00:02:09.033
English Christmas is lovely.

00:02:09.033 --> 00:02:12.067
You go, you put your roast in,
then you go to a bar.

00:02:12.067 --> 00:02:13.234
-Great.

00:02:13.234 --> 00:02:16.067
-Because there's a lot
of alcoholics out there.

00:02:16.067 --> 00:02:17.200
-Yeah, yeah.

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:18.868
-So we went
to this beautiful pub,

00:02:18.868 --> 00:02:21.000
and there was
all these people there,

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:24.234
and we're in Richmond,
where "Ted Lasso" takes place.

00:02:24.234 --> 00:02:26.167
You're overlooking
the beautiful village green.

00:02:26.167 --> 00:02:27.200
It's gorgeous.
-That's great.

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:28.667
And you were with family?

00:02:28.667 --> 00:02:31.300
-I was with my wife's
entire family, okay?

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:33.000
I'm Jewish.
My wife's not.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:35.601
So her Christian family and me
in England,

00:02:35.601 --> 00:02:38.834
but I feel comfortable.
-Yeah, although it's weird,

00:02:38.834 --> 00:02:41.734
'cause you're making
a very clear distinction.

00:02:41.734 --> 00:02:44.868
-Yes. Yeah, no,
I swear, it was great.

00:02:44.868 --> 00:02:47.934
And we're there,
and we're outside,

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:50.400
and this British woman
comes up to me.

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:52.100
Like I said,
I'd been getting recognized.

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:54.734
-Yeah, Mr. Worldwide.
-Mr. Worldwide.

00:02:54.734 --> 00:02:57.767
And she kind of, you know,
has that smile on her face,

00:02:57.767 --> 00:03:00.200
and she's holding her phone,
which is turned to the camera.

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:02.701
She's kind of looking at me.
And I was like, "Picture?"

00:03:02.701 --> 00:03:04.901
She goes, "Yeah."
And I go, "What's your name?"

00:03:04.901 --> 00:03:07.200
And she's like, "Pat."
And I'm like, "Hello, Pat.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:09.567
I'm Ike," and I grab it
and I put my arm around her

00:03:09.567 --> 00:03:10.701
and I get into selfie mode.

00:03:10.701 --> 00:03:11.968
I'm like, "Are you having
a good Christmas?"

00:03:11.968 --> 00:03:13.167
She's like, "Yeah."

00:03:13.167 --> 00:03:15.033
I'm like, "Let's get one.
Let's get a fun one."

00:03:15.033 --> 00:03:16.667
You know,
and I give it back to her.

00:03:16.667 --> 00:03:18.434
I'm like, "Thank you, Pat.
Have a great Christmas."

00:03:18.434 --> 00:03:19.868
She goes, "Thank you.

00:03:19.868 --> 00:03:22.467
Will you take a photo of me
and my family, please?"

00:03:22.467 --> 00:03:25.000
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:27.701
And...

00:03:27.701 --> 00:03:30.601
as my brain is processing
what's happening,

00:03:30.601 --> 00:03:32.701
just like six degrees
to the right,

00:03:32.701 --> 00:03:36.834
my wife is crying, like,
the hardest she's ever laughed.

00:03:36.834 --> 00:03:38.701
Runs over
to her whole family like,

00:03:38.701 --> 00:03:40.767
"You're not going to believe
what just happened."

00:03:40.767 --> 00:03:42.567
So the rest of the trip,
like, the nephews are like,

00:03:42.567 --> 00:03:44.567
"Hey, remember
when that lady..."

00:03:44.567 --> 00:03:47.200
And I'm like, "Yeah."
-Also, it really --

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:49.534
It shows you that the politeness
of the British people

00:03:49.534 --> 00:03:51.601
can do a great disservice,
'cause any other country,

00:03:51.601 --> 00:03:52.701
they'd be like,
"No, no, not with you."

00:03:52.701 --> 00:03:54.067
-"Who are you?
No, no, no, no."

00:03:54.067 --> 00:03:56.434
-But she let you go through
with two photos.

00:03:56.434 --> 00:03:58.234
You did the fun one.
-And a fun one.

00:03:58.234 --> 00:03:59.667
-Yeah.
-So embarrassing.

00:03:59.667 --> 00:04:03.400
She's going to, like,
someday see something I'm in

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:06.467
and be like, "Oh, he took
a photo with me once.

00:04:06.467 --> 00:04:09.033
Remember that weirdo in the park
on Christmas?"

00:04:09.033 --> 00:04:10.267
-That'll be fun, too.
She'll be like,

00:04:10.267 --> 00:04:14.000
"Here he is being serious,
and here's his fun one."

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:15.400
But look, you know what?

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:17.567
All jokes aside,
congratulations, my friend.

00:04:17.567 --> 00:04:18.734
You did it.
-Oh, look at that.

00:04:18.734 --> 00:04:21.133
-You did it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:21.133 --> 00:04:24.601
-Right there.
-I mean, I --

00:04:24.601 --> 00:04:26.300
I spent a couple summers

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:27.801
where I fully was
a roommate of yours,

00:04:27.801 --> 00:04:31.267
and I know you to be a guy
who would come home every day,

00:04:31.267 --> 00:04:34.734
watch "Jeopardy!", yell out the
answers before the contestants.

00:04:34.734 --> 00:04:36.801
-Yes, very annoying.
-And a lot of people do that,

00:04:36.801 --> 00:04:38.901
and it's very annoying
and it goes nowhere,

00:04:38.901 --> 00:04:40.400
and they live sad lives,

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:43.267
and yet you're, like,
the one guy

00:04:43.267 --> 00:04:46.567
where you basically can turn
around and just flip us all off

00:04:46.567 --> 00:04:48.200
and be like,
"See, I was studying!"

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:50.734
-Celebrity champion!
Celebrity champion!

00:04:50.734 --> 00:04:51.834
Yeah, it was amazing.

00:04:51.834 --> 00:04:53.834
-Were you nervous
about your competition?

00:04:53.834 --> 00:04:55.033
-I was pretty nervous.

00:04:55.033 --> 00:04:57.300
There were a couple names
on the list of celebs.

00:04:57.300 --> 00:04:59.734
Our good friend Brendan Hunt.
-Yeah, from "Ted Lasso."

00:04:59.734 --> 00:05:03.167
-From "Ted Lasso," was
very worried about playing him.

00:05:03.167 --> 00:05:06.334
Patton Oswalt, I was
very worried about playing him.

00:05:06.334 --> 00:05:07.501
-Very heady,
very smart gentleman.

00:05:07.501 --> 00:05:09.934
-Very smart guy,
and it came down, basically,

00:05:09.934 --> 00:05:13.200
to me and him in the finals,
and I beat him by $1.

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:15.167
-That's very exciting.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:15.167 --> 00:05:19.968
Now, you go on, correct --
Now, I didn't realize this.

00:05:19.968 --> 00:05:22.534
You play in the Tournament
of Champions with regular --

00:05:22.534 --> 00:05:25.067
-Yes, the non-celebrities.

00:05:25.067 --> 00:05:27.033
-'Cause I won
celebrity poker once,

00:05:27.033 --> 00:05:29.367
and people always would say,
"Oh, that's so impressive."

00:05:29.367 --> 00:05:30.534
And I'm saying,
you have to remember,

00:05:30.534 --> 00:05:32.567
when you put "celebrity"
in front of a contest,

00:05:32.567 --> 00:05:34.234
it's a way of saying worse.
-Yes.

00:05:34.234 --> 00:05:36.267
-Are you worried about this one,

00:05:36.267 --> 00:05:38.033
or you just kind of go in
knowing you have no chance?

00:05:38.033 --> 00:05:39.734
-Oh, I'm terrified.

00:05:39.734 --> 00:05:41.067
I'm going to get my ass

00:05:41.067 --> 00:05:44.267
absolutely handed to me
by just --

00:05:44.267 --> 00:05:46.868
I have no plan.
I have no plan.

00:05:46.868 --> 00:05:49.868
I would try to bully them,
but that won't work.

00:05:49.868 --> 00:05:52.868
And I'm just going to get
destroyed, and I can't wait.

00:05:52.868 --> 00:05:55.133
I can't wait.
-I hope -- You know what?

00:05:55.133 --> 00:05:57.200
I hope that night
is the first time

00:05:57.200 --> 00:05:59.834
that woman whose picture
you took sees you.

00:05:59.834 --> 00:06:01.267
-[ British accent ]
Oh, God. The guy --

00:06:01.267 --> 00:06:04.501
That bloke with the -$2,000,
look, look at the fun one.

00:06:04.501 --> 00:06:06.634
-[ British accent ]
He always thinks he's there

00:06:06.634 --> 00:06:08.868
for the wrong thing.

00:06:08.868 --> 00:06:10.801
[ Normal voice] I want to ask
about "History of the World."

00:06:10.801 --> 00:06:12.801
We'll be right back with more
from Ike Barinholtz.

